T ThemeColour            | ThemeSpecification.h | 28-32   | contract,nonallocating,nonthrowing | -  | One interface colour: a coordinate carrying the space it is a coordinate in, plus the fraction it covers. colour whose space nothing states is the shape a transfer function is later added to "fix". Held as a `ColourSpecification` in the display space so the absence of any transfer inside `SlateUI` stays checkable. fraction over the interface's own recording, not a property of the colour — `36` carries no alpha for exactly that reason.
    has   Coordinate  ColourSpecification  [-]  ?
    has   Coverage    double               [-]  ?
    by    Api/ControlPanel.h, Source/ChannelPanel.cpp, Source/ControlChoice.cpp, Source/ControlChrome.cpp, Source/ControlInterior.h, Source/ControlLayout.cpp, (+7 more)
    note  🔴 `36` §1 and `14` §5 together: a packed integer would be a bare triple whose space nothing states, and a
    note  ⚠️ Coverage is not part of `ColourSpecification` and never becomes part of it. Coverage is a compositing

F Quantize               | ThemeSpecification.h | 42      | api,nonallocating,nonthrowing      | ✔️ | Quantises one theme colour to the eight-bit-per-channel code the vendor draw surface accepts. Coordinates outside the unit interval are bounded here rather than wrapping, because a wrapped code is a colour the artist sees as a wrong hue rather than as a clipped one.
    in    Colour  const ThemeColour&  [-]  the colour, coordinates read in the display space
    out   -       Code                [-]  packed as red in the low byte, then green, blue and coverage
    by    Source/ControlLayout.cpp, Source/ThemeSpecification.cpp, Source/WorkspaceStrip.cpp
    note  🔴 The only place a theme colour becomes a bare integer, and it is a quantisation and not a projection.

F Attenuate              | ThemeSpecification.h | 50      | api,nonallocating,nonthrowing      | ✔️ | Returns one theme colour at a declared coverage, its coordinate untouched.
    in    Colour            ThemeColour  [-]  the colour to re-cover
    in    DeclaredCoverage  double       [-]  the fraction, bounded to the unit interval
    out   -                 ThemeColour  [-]  ?
    by    Source/ChannelPanel.cpp, Source/ControlLayout.cpp, Source/DiagnosticPanel.cpp, Source/LayerPanel.cpp, Source/PropertyPanel.cpp, Source/RevisionPanel.cpp, (+2 more)
    note  What a hover tint or a disabled row is — the same colour at less coverage, never a second literal.

